    "narrative": "The LawDog offensive outlook for May 21 features **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Tyler Freeman** as our top-tier plays, boasting scores of 67.55 and 67.23, respectively. **Geraldo Perdomo** benefits from a high-efficiency matchup against Agnos, with his score inflated significantly by a favorable SP skill profile (+19%) and a premium #3 lineup spot. Similarly, **Tyler Freeman** capitalizes on an attractive encounter with Rodriguez, Ed, where the combination of a favorable park factor and a top-of-the-order slot makes him a foundational piece for today\u2019s 5x5 run production. While **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a staple with a 66.16 rating, we must remain cautious of his matchup against Mize; the park factors are helpful, but we are discounting his floor slightly due to a 40% SB prevention rate from the opponent's battery, which threatens his upside in our scarcest category.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involves **Lawrence Butler**, who sits on the fringes of our starting threshold with a 54.21 score. While his platoon advantage against Soriano, J (+13%) is notable, the detrimental impact of his #9 lineup placement (-8%) prevents him from moving into the \"Strong\" start tier. He remains our primary pivot should any late-scratch lineup news improve his projected batting order. We are continuing to monitor the health of **Cal Raleigh**, who remains sidelined on the IL, while **Will Smith**, **Bryson Stott**, and **Taylor Ward** are effectively locked out due to team off-days. We will rely on our depth, including **Yainer Diaz**, **Jonathan Aranda**, **Matt Chapman**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Luis Arraez**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Gavin Sheets**, and **Drew Gilbert** to manage our game caps as the week progresses. **Daulton Varsho** is the only player in today's lineup carrying a distinct platoon risk (-10%), making him our highest variance candidate against Rod\u00f3n.",
